{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe single-pass review system was a demo the project has been retiring; the real reviews are the four-phase plan review and four-phase code review, whose single-turn criteria are steps inside those workflows (operator ruling 2026-09-06). `src/rebar/llm/operations.py:135-218 _review_ticket_impl` (plus `_REVIEW_MIN_STEPS` and its explanatory comment `:35-42`, `default_reviewer_id:45-54`, docstring `:1-17`) survives only for two callers: `src/rebar/llm/review_workflows.py:70 diff_review_paths` (the WS-K2 parallel-run-and-diff; it calls the engine at `:86`; sole importer `tests/interfaces/store/test_review_as_workflow.py:14`) and `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:406-414` (the `ticket-quality` branch). `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/ticket_quality.md` is the prompt behind `reviewers/index.json:80-92` (`\"default\": true` at `:84`, langfuse `rebar-ticket-quality`), the eval spec `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/ticket-quality.eval.yaml`, and `src/rebar/llm/workflow/examples/review_skeleton.yaml:31`. It is the catalog's ONLY default reviewer; `src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py:291` raises unless EXACTLY ONE default exists, and `select_reviewers` (`prompts.py:620`, re-exported `operations.py:27`, public via `rebar.llm.__init__.py:59,127`) unions every default, so a replacement default is required. `rebar.llm` is NOT in `scripts/gen_api_surface.py:54-62 MODULES`, so removing the `aggregate_findings` export does not move `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` (its `select_reviewers:2306` entry belongs to `rebar.llm.prompting.prompts` and is untouched). `docs/release-notes.md:946` records the earlier decision to keep the engine. `src/rebar/llm/aggregate.py` (125 LOC) is the ADR-0075-orphaned multi-reviewer aggregator: `aggregate_findings` has no src caller (ADR 0108 `:123`) but `src/rebar/llm/spec_scan.py:13,137` imports `_severity_rank`. Proof the four-phase workflows are untouched: `git grep -n \"ticket-quality\\|ticket_quality\" origin/main -- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json src/rebar/llm/code_review/ src/rebar/llm/criteria/ 'src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_*.md' 'src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-*.md' .rebar/criteria_routing.json` returns zero hits, and `workflow/gates/code-review.yaml:71-108,126-148` prompt ids are all `code-review-*`. Cites re-measured on origin/main e2ed08b343a by whole-tree per-symbol sweep, not sampling.\n\n## Approach\n1. `operations.py`: rewrite docstring `:1-17` as \"the shared deterministic context builder for the gates, plus the `select_reviewers` re-export\"; delete `:35-42` (comment + `_REVIEW_MIN_STEPS`), `:45-54` (`default_reviewer_id`), `:135-218` (`_review_ticket_impl`, to EOF); `__all__:33` becomes `[\"assemble_context\", \"select_reviewers\"]`; keep the `TYPE_CHECKING` `PrefetchSpec` import; drop the unused `replace`, `LLMError`, `Runner`, `RunRequest`, `get_runner`, `resolve_gate_config` imports.\n2. `git rm src/rebar/llm/review_workflows.py src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/ticket-quality.eval.yaml src/rebar/llm/reviewers/ticket_quality.md`.\n3. `eval_solver.py:406-414` delete the branch; drop the `operations` import if it becomes unused.\n4. `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code_quality.md:12` `default: false` becomes `default: true` — it is the code-review rules layer's natural always-on reviewer, and `applies_to` is empty for both prompts, so `default` is the only selector in play. Run `python -m rebar.llm.prompting.prompts regenerate-index` (CI drift gate, `docs/llm-framework.md:399`): `ticket-quality` leaves `index.json` and `code-quality` carries `\"default\": true`.\n5. `review_skeleton.yaml:31` becomes `- prompt: spec-alignment` — the only surviving `category: review` prompt whose subject is ticket or plan text (the skeleton's input is `plan`) and not already used (`code-quality` is the batch finder at `:29`, `completion-verifier` the verifier at `:42`), so the sample keeps two always-on criteria plus one `when`-gated. Mirror at `docs/workflow-engine.md:103`.\n6. `aggregate.py`: move `_SEVERITY_RANK` and `_severity_rank` (`:19-24`) into `spec_scan.py` as private helpers, replacing the import at `:13` (the only `spec_scan.py` edit); `git rm src/rebar/llm/aggregate.py`; delete `src/rebar/llm/__init__.py:36` and `:106`; fix the comments at `code_review/workflow_ops.py:24,150` (\"mirrors aggregate.py\" becomes \"10-line bucket\").\n7. Retire the dead ids everywhere AC1 greps, so the plan can satisfy its own criterion: `docs/llm-framework.md:692` \"→ `aggregate_findings` —\" becomes \"→ a findings aggregator —\" (b744 history survives; the dead name does not); `prompts.py:153` and `docs/reuse-surface.md:311` change their id-normalization example to ``code_quality.md`` → ``code-quality``; `docs/llm-framework.md:355` sample `\"reviewers\": [\"ticket-quality\"]` becomes `[\"spec-alignment\"]`; `tests/unit/test_new_eval_specs.py:2` drops `ticket-quality` from its docstring; `src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py:80` drops `\"ticket-quality\"` from `AGENTIC_SOLVERS` — pulled IN scope because the id ceases to exist and AC1 covers `src`. ADRs and `docs/release-notes.md` are AC1-excluded and keep their history verbatim.\n8. `docs/release-notes.md` new entry: \"BREAKING (pre-1.0): the single-pass review engine and `rebar.llm.aggregate_findings` are removed. `rebar.llm.operations._review_ticket_impl` (private), the packaged `ticket-quality` reviewer prompt (Langfuse name `rebar-ticket-quality`) and its eval spec, and the public `rebar.llm.aggregate_findings` export are gone; `code-quality` is now the catalog's default reviewer, so `rebar.llm.select_reviewers([])` returns `[\"code-quality\"]`. Use `rebar.llm.review_plan`.\" (`rebar.llm` is the \"less settled\" row, `docs/api-stability.md:28`.)\n\n## Scope\nThe files above. Out of scope: `assemble_context` (live consumer `workflow/gate_ops.py:192`), `completion.py`, and `spec_scan.py` beyond the 3-line helper move. Nothing defers to the eval-harness epic: `provider_parity.py:80` is handled in step 7 because AC1 would otherwise fail on it.\n\n## Testing\nOne test file is deleted (`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_review_budget.py`; both its tests are the retired step floor; the completion-side floor is covered by `test_completion_budget.py`'s `verify_step_floor` tests), one is renamed (`test_review_as_workflow.py` to `test_runner_agent_step_bridge.py`), eleven tests are rewritten against `spec_scan.scan_epics_for_spec` (the structural sibling with the same `gate_source` threading and `runner=` seam), the `ticket-quality` id is swapped to `code-quality` in stand-in uses, and golden sets drop it. `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py:532` `assert len(_EXPECTED_RUN_REQUEST_SITES) == 21` becomes `== 20` when the `_review_ticket_impl` row at `:486` goes. The exact per-file list is in this ticket's first comment, as corrected by its third. Happy path: `select_reviewers([])` returns `['code-quality']` and the skeleton workflow validates. Edge: the regenerate-index drift gate is clean and the catalog has exactly one default.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git grep -n \"_review_ticket_impl\\|review_workflows\\|ticket-quality\\|ticket_quality\\|rebar-ticket-quality\\|aggregate_findings\" -- src tests docs scripts ':!docs/release-notes.md' ':!docs/adr' ':!docs/experiments' ':!tests/fixtures'` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.llm.prompting.prompts regenerate-index && git diff --exit-code src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json` is clean and `index.json` has exactly one `\"default\": true` (`code-quality`), asserted by `tests/unit/test_prompt_index.py::test_index_has_exactly_one_default`.\n- [ ] `python -c \"import rebar.llm as l; print(l.select_reviewers([]))\"` prints `['code-quality']`.\n- [ ] `rebar workflow validate src/rebar/llm/workflow/examples/review_skeleton.yaml` is clean and `tests/unit/workflow/test_review_skeleton.py` is green.\n- [ ] The workflow-untouched grep (context section) still prints zero hits.\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --check` is clean; `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793229889616172770,"uuid":"7296dab3-a6eb-426f-b819-527f9bd45c93"}